**La Gaulette** stretches along the coast road between Case Noyale and Le Morne with green mountain slopes behind it and the lagoon in front. It has kept the feel of a fishing village with small shops and pirogues pulled up on the shore and a slower pace than the resorts further south.

## Île aux Bénitiers and the Crystal Rock

About 1.5 km offshore lies Île aux Bénitiers. It is a low coral islet of some 65 hectares once known as Île du Morne and its beaches look straight across the lagoon to Le Morne Brabant. Nearby the Crystal Rock is an exposed fossil coral reef rising from clear shallow water and has become one of the most photographed sights in Mauritius. Boat trips from La Gaulette and the neighbouring villages usually combine the two.

## The lagoon

The wide lagoon between La Gaulette and Le Morne is a favourite with kitesurfers and windsurfers especially in the windier months of the southern winter. Beginners stay on the flat water inside the reef; the waves on the reef itself are for experts only.

## The road to Chamarel

Just north of La Gaulette at Case Noyale a winding road climbs into the hills towards Chamarel. The viewpoint on the way up looks down on the lagoon and Île aux Bénitiers and Le Morne. It is one of the finest views on the island.

## Getting there

La Gaulette is roughly an hour and a quarter by car from the international airport either along the west coast or across the south via Baie du Cap.

## Good to know

- Boat trips are best in the morning when the water is calm and the light clear.
- Bring reef shoes for wading around the islet and the Crystal Rock.
